was evidence of a conditioned fear being respond, being conditioned there. So this would happen. repeatedly, so over a number of different trials, and this would essentially result in an association be informed that when this rat is present, there's a really unpleasant or aversive thing that happens, a loud noise which couldn't be explained. That research has been a sort of foundation for lots of the models and theories that have developed since in order to try and treat phobias and provide effective therapeutic interventions, and extinction learning is absolutely critical to that. trying to be achieved in extinction learning is to remove or replace that association that's been formed, that the rat suddenly symbolizes something which is aversive in the environment.
